CEL + internal/filter; Each dialect driver calls `filter.DefaultEngine()` and `filter.AppendConditions`, which compiles the CEL string with `cel-go`, builds a dialect-agnostic condition tree, and renders it to dialect-specific SQL placeholders via `render.go`, appending the fragments to the query's `WHERE` clause.

The `ListMemos` `filter` field is documented as a **CEL expression** in `proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto`:

```326:338:proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto
  // Optional. A CEL expression to filter memos. Combine terms with && and ||.
  // Available fields:
  //   content (string), creator (string, e.g. "users/1"),
  //   created_ts / updated_ts (timestamp), pinned (bool),
  //   visibility (string: PRIVATE | PROTECTED | PUBLIC),
  //   tags (list<string>; match with `"work" in tags`, not `tag == "work"`),
  //   has_task_list / has_link / has_code / has_incomplete_tasks (bool).
```

The engine lives in **`internal/filter/`** (core files: `engine.go`, `parser.go`, `schema.go`, `ir.go`, `render.go`, `helpers.go`). `Engine` uses **`github.com/google/cel-go/cel`** to compile filters:

```13:14:internal/filter/engine.go
